1
00:00:00,649 --> 00:00:00,929
"Lucas…

2
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:01,530
it's me.

3
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:03,330
Sorry for the late hour." "I found her.

4
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:06,029
She's in all the photos." "And she knows…

5
00:00:06,049 --> 00:00:10,169
that I know." That was the last message Rafael left

6
00:00:10,189 --> 00:00:11,689
on his brother's phone.

7
00:00:11,709 --> 00:00:14,379
At three-forty in the morning.

8
00:00:14,429 --> 00:00:16,910
When Lucas arrived in the morning,

9
00:00:16,929 --> 00:00:19,669
the apartment door was locked from the inside.

10
00:00:19,689 --> 00:00:22,200
And Rafael wasn't there.

11
00:00:26,789 --> 00:00:28,280
Good evening.

12
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,520
Welcome back to Último Abrigo.

13
00:00:31,769 --> 00:00:34,759
Answer me something, truthfully.

14
00:00:34,850 --> 00:00:36,869
Have you ever felt…

15
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:39,649
someone walking behind you?

16
00:00:39,670 --> 00:00:41,660
Inside your own house?

17
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:44,890
That chill in the hallway.

18
00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:46,950
The certainty that, if you turn around right now,

19
00:00:46,970 --> 00:00:48,800
there'll be someone there.

20
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:50,350
And you turn around.

21
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:51,980
And there's no one there.

22
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:54,630
Everyone has felt that.

23
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:57,149
And today I'm going to tell you the story of a man who decided

24
00:00:57,170 --> 00:00:59,340
to find out why.

25
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:01,810
In twenty fourteen, in Switzerland,

26
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:05,390
a group of scientists conducted a curious experiment.

27
00:01:05,409 --> 00:01:07,390
The volunteers were blindfolded,

28
00:01:07,409 --> 00:01:09,970
moving a robotic arm in front of their body.

29
00:01:09,990 --> 00:01:11,670
And a second robot, behind them,

30
00:01:11,689 --> 00:01:13,850
touched each person's back.

31
00:01:13,870 --> 00:01:16,059
With a half-second delay.

32
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:19,119
Many began to feel someone behind them.

33
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:23,319
Some reported two, three, four presences.

34
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:25,719
Some even asked to stop.

35
00:01:26,269 --> 00:01:29,670
The scientists' conclusion was simple: it's the brain.

36
00:01:29,689 --> 00:01:32,679
A delay between what the body does and what it feels.

37
00:01:32,769 --> 00:01:34,179
Nothing beyond that.

38
00:01:34,689 --> 00:01:37,059
Nothing beyond that.

39
00:01:37,450 --> 00:01:40,550
Rafael was thirty-four years old.

40
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:41,870
A sound technician.

41
00:01:41,890 --> 00:01:43,930
He lived alone in an old apartment,

42
00:01:43,950 --> 00:01:47,219
on the third floor, at the end of a quiet street.

43
00:01:48,010 --> 00:01:51,500
And ever since he was a kid, he felt that.

44
00:01:51,829 --> 00:01:54,070
The first time was at his grandmother's house,

45
00:01:54,090 --> 00:01:55,140
in the countryside.

46
00:01:55,790 --> 00:01:58,890
A long hallway with creaky floorboards,

47
00:01:58,909 --> 00:02:01,699
connecting the kitchen to the bedrooms.

48
00:02:02,250 --> 00:02:04,640
He was about seven years old.

49
00:02:04,909 --> 00:02:06,530
He'd run through that hallway,

50
00:02:06,549 --> 00:02:11,340
every night, certain that someone was coming behind him.

51
00:02:11,909 --> 00:02:14,239
Once, he told his grandmother.

52
00:02:14,549 --> 00:02:15,799
She didn't laugh.

53
00:02:15,909 --> 00:02:20,010
She just held his face with both hands and said,

54
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:24,239
very seriously: "Don't go looking, my son.

55
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:26,000
He who doesn't look…

56
00:02:26,030 --> 00:02:31,069
doesn't find." He never understood what she meant.

57
00:02:31,089 --> 00:02:33,159
Until many years later.

58
00:02:34,669 --> 00:02:36,579
In the beginning, it was rare.

59
00:02:36,810 --> 00:02:40,000
One night or another, watching television,

60
00:02:40,049 --> 00:02:42,539
he would feel someone's gaze on the back of his neck.

61
00:02:42,889 --> 00:02:45,250
But it was in the hallway that it all really started.

62
00:02:45,269 --> 00:02:48,490
The apartment had a long hallway,

63
00:02:48,509 --> 00:02:50,159
from the living room to the bedroom.

64
00:02:50,209 --> 00:02:52,909
And every time he walked through there at night,

65
00:02:52,929 --> 00:02:54,639
he felt someone coming behind him.

66
00:02:54,989 --> 00:02:56,259
He would stop.

67
00:02:56,489 --> 00:02:58,280
The silence stopped with him.

68
00:02:58,569 --> 00:03:00,280
And whenever he turned around…

69
00:03:00,389 --> 00:03:02,400
the hallway was empty.

70
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:04,719
Do a test right now.

71
00:03:05,409 --> 00:03:06,919
Don't look back.

72
00:03:07,250 --> 00:03:09,400
Just pay attention to the back of your neck.

73
00:03:10,129 --> 00:03:11,379
Feel it?

74
00:03:12,109 --> 00:03:15,599
Over time, the feeling stopped being rare.

75
00:03:16,069 --> 00:03:17,539
Every night.

76
00:03:17,810 --> 00:03:20,409
In the kitchen, opening the fridge.

77
00:03:20,429 --> 00:03:21,650
In the shower.

78
00:03:21,669 --> 00:03:23,199
Lying down.

79
00:03:23,449 --> 00:03:26,060
And the worst part wasn't feeling someone behind him.

80
00:03:26,169 --> 00:03:28,759
The worst part was feeling that, with every night,

81
00:03:28,909 --> 00:03:30,919
it was a little bit closer.

82
00:03:31,389 --> 00:03:32,799
closer.

83
00:03:33,549 --> 00:03:36,259
He started hearing things.

84
00:03:36,409 --> 00:03:41,060
Footsteps in the hallway that stopped half a second after his.

85
00:03:41,209 --> 00:03:45,199
A slow breathing, right after he turned off the light.

86
00:03:46,489 --> 00:03:50,219
As a sound technician, he did what he knew how to do.

87
00:03:50,549 --> 00:03:53,050
He left a professional microphone running in the hallway all

88
00:03:53,069 --> 00:03:54,359
night long.

89
00:03:54,569 --> 00:03:58,400
In the morning, he put on his headphones and listened.

90
00:03:58,609 --> 00:04:00,909
Hours of silence.

91
00:04:00,929 --> 00:04:03,189
His footsteps going to the bathroom,

92
00:04:03,209 --> 00:04:04,430
at two in the morning.

93
00:04:04,449 --> 00:04:07,680
And, right after each of his steps…

94
00:04:07,989 --> 00:04:09,199
another step.

95
00:04:09,389 --> 00:04:10,519
Lighter.

96
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,500
Half a second delayed.

97
00:04:12,789 --> 00:04:15,819
He listened to that section about twenty times.

98
00:04:16,269 --> 00:04:19,790
When he stopped in the hallway, the other steps stopped

99
00:04:19,810 --> 00:04:20,800
too.

100
00:04:20,949 --> 00:04:24,820
Except, the last time, when he had already gone back to bed…

101
00:04:25,050 --> 00:04:26,900
the footsteps kept going.

102
00:04:27,110 --> 00:04:28,360
Slowly.

103
00:04:28,569 --> 00:04:30,460
All the way to the bedroom door.

104
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,090
He went to the doctor.

105
00:04:32,110 --> 00:04:33,120
Got tests done.

106
00:04:33,139 --> 00:04:34,879
Everything was normal.

107
00:04:35,089 --> 00:04:37,829
The doctor prescribed sleeping pills and said it was

108
00:04:37,849 --> 00:04:38,990
stress.

109
00:04:39,009 --> 00:04:40,420
Exhaustion.

110
00:04:40,509 --> 00:04:42,720
The medication made him sleep.

111
00:04:42,889 --> 00:04:45,340
But it didn't make the feeling go away.

112
00:04:45,629 --> 00:04:49,329
It was during one of those late nights that he found the Swiss study.

113
00:04:49,349 --> 00:04:52,310
And, for the first time in months, he felt relief.

114
00:04:52,329 --> 00:04:54,009
It was his brain.

115
00:04:54,029 --> 00:04:54,990
That was all.

116
00:04:55,009 --> 00:04:56,920
A half-second delay.

117
00:04:57,029 --> 00:04:59,120
For a few days, it worked.

118
00:04:59,149 --> 00:05:00,470
He slept better.

119
00:05:00,490 --> 00:05:02,840
He walked down the hallway without looking back.

120
00:05:03,069 --> 00:05:06,490
Until the night when, brushing his teeth,

121
00:05:06,509 --> 00:05:08,340
he felt the back of his neck go cold.

122
00:05:08,709 --> 00:05:10,600
It wasn't a chill.

123
00:05:10,829 --> 00:05:11,550
It was cold.

124
00:05:11,569 --> 00:05:14,629
As if someone were breathing right there,

125
00:05:14,649 --> 00:05:16,700
inches away from him.

126
00:05:16,789 --> 00:05:18,560
He didn't turn around.

127
00:05:18,589 --> 00:05:22,240
For the first time, he was afraid to turn around.

128
00:05:22,529 --> 00:05:26,020
After that night, Rafael changed the whole house.

129
00:05:26,129 --> 00:05:28,490
Pushed all the furniture against the walls.

130
00:05:28,509 --> 00:05:30,110
Left the lights on.

131
00:05:30,129 --> 00:05:33,600
Put mirrors in the corners to see what was coming behind him.

132
00:05:33,810 --> 00:05:37,760
And started sleeping sitting up, his back to the wall.

133
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:40,800
But the feeling wouldn't go away.

134
00:05:41,050 --> 00:05:42,230
It just kept getting closer.

135
00:05:42,250 --> 00:05:45,530
One Sunday, his brother, Lucas,

136
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:47,360
showed up unannounced.

137
00:05:47,389 --> 00:05:49,700
Found the apartment strange.

138
00:05:49,849 --> 00:05:53,560
The furniture pressed against the walls, the mirrors,

139
00:05:53,629 --> 00:05:56,360
the lights on in broad daylight.

140
00:05:56,829 --> 00:05:58,680
Rafael tried to explain.

141
00:05:59,050 --> 00:06:00,970
Lucas laughed, a bit awkwardly.

142
00:06:00,990 --> 00:06:02,870
Said he needed to sleep,

143
00:06:02,889 --> 00:06:05,520
get out a bit, see people.

144
00:06:05,930 --> 00:06:08,900
When it was time to leave, in the middle of the hallway,

145
00:06:08,990 --> 00:06:10,590
Lucas stopped.

146
00:06:10,610 --> 00:06:12,720
Ran his hand over the back of his neck.

147
00:06:13,329 --> 00:06:14,530
"Man…

148
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:18,700
what kind of draft is this?" Rafael didn't answer.

149
00:06:18,769 --> 00:06:19,689
He just opened the door.

150
00:06:19,709 --> 00:06:21,960
And waited for his brother to leave.

151
00:06:22,170 --> 00:06:25,269
On a sleepless night, he posted on an internet

152
00:06:25,289 --> 00:06:26,280
forum.

153
00:06:26,449 --> 00:06:29,060
Asked if anyone else felt that.

154
00:06:29,229 --> 00:06:32,980
Someone walking behind them, closer every night.

155
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:36,230
In a few hours, dozens of replies came in.

156
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:38,689
People from all over Brazil.

157
00:06:38,709 --> 00:06:40,200
From other countries.

158
00:06:40,550 --> 00:06:43,460
Everyone describing the exact same thing.

159
00:06:43,629 --> 00:06:45,900
One reply caught his attention.

160
00:06:46,009 --> 00:06:48,790
A user who signed with only their initials.

161
00:06:48,810 --> 00:06:51,949
He said he had found a way to prove it.

162
00:06:51,969 --> 00:06:55,370
That he was going to take photos of the house every night and compare them.

163
00:06:55,389 --> 00:06:58,209
Rafael replied, asking him to share whatever he

164
00:06:58,229 --> 00:06:59,500
found.

165
00:06:59,649 --> 00:07:02,430
Three days later, a final message arrived.

166
00:07:02,449 --> 00:07:04,580
Just one sentence.

167
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:07,990
"Don't look for her." After that,

168
00:07:08,009 --> 00:07:10,220
the account never replied again.

169
00:07:10,269 --> 00:07:13,000
A bit of trivia, since we're here.

170
00:07:13,170 --> 00:07:16,129
Each of your eyes has a blind spot.

171
00:07:16,149 --> 00:07:18,329
A spot where the optic nerve leaves the eye,

172
00:07:18,349 --> 00:07:21,449
and where you, literally, see nothing.

173
00:07:21,469 --> 00:07:23,620
You never notice it.

174
00:07:23,689 --> 00:07:26,769
Because your brain paints over that hole with what it thinks

175
00:07:26,789 --> 00:07:27,730
should be there.

176
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:29,650
In other words…

177
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:33,110
it hides from you what you can't see.

178
00:07:33,129 --> 00:07:34,420
Keep that in mind.

179
00:07:34,649 --> 00:07:37,910
When we're afraid of something we can't see…

180
00:07:37,930 --> 00:07:39,360
what do we do?

181
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:42,480
We try to prove it doesn't exist.

182
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:45,160
That's what Rafael decided to do.

183
00:07:45,370 --> 00:07:47,990
Every night, he started photographing the house.

184
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:49,090
Every room.

185
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:51,520
The same angle, at the same time.

186
00:07:51,589 --> 00:07:53,170
The idea was simple.

187
00:07:53,189 --> 00:07:54,790
If the photos didn't show anything,

188
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:57,910
the feeling was all in his head.

189
00:07:57,930 --> 00:07:59,939
And he'd be able to forget.

190
00:08:00,469 --> 00:08:01,910
Weeks went by.

191
00:08:01,930 --> 00:08:03,500
Hundreds of photos.

192
00:08:03,769 --> 00:08:07,090
One night, he printed them all out and spread them across the

193
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:07,819
table.

194
00:08:07,839 --> 00:08:09,610
To look carefully.

195
00:08:09,629 --> 00:08:11,449
To prove, once and for all,

196
00:08:11,469 --> 00:08:13,540
that there was nothing there.

197
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:15,230
And for a long time…

198
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:16,300
there wasn't.

199
00:08:16,389 --> 00:08:19,129
Until he stopped on a photo of the street.

200
00:08:19,149 --> 00:08:22,050
Way in the back, past the last streetlight,

201
00:08:22,069 --> 00:08:23,290
between two trees.

202
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:25,069
A shape.

203
00:08:25,089 --> 00:08:26,829
Tall.

204
00:08:26,849 --> 00:08:28,660
Too thin.

205
00:08:28,990 --> 00:08:30,040
Motionless.

206
00:08:30,490 --> 00:08:32,129
He picked up the next photo.

207
00:08:32,150 --> 00:08:32,669
The one of the living room.

208
00:08:32,690 --> 00:08:34,399
And looked for it.

209
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:36,009
It was there.

210
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:37,860
In the reflection of the window.

211
00:08:37,930 --> 00:08:39,379
In the hallway.

212
00:08:39,690 --> 00:08:41,600
In the kitchen doorway.

213
00:08:41,770 --> 00:08:43,700
In the corner of the bedroom.

214
00:08:43,930 --> 00:08:45,360
In all of them.

215
00:08:46,170 --> 00:08:47,899
And with each photo…

216
00:08:48,050 --> 00:08:50,139
a little bit closer.

217
00:08:50,330 --> 00:08:50,949
in all of them.

218
00:08:50,970 --> 00:08:54,409
Rafael grabbed a red pen.

219
00:08:54,430 --> 00:08:57,860
And, with a trembling hand, circled each one.

220
00:08:57,970 --> 00:09:02,320
When he finished, he realized the scariest thing of all.

221
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:05,600
That had never been just a feeling.

222
00:09:05,950 --> 00:09:07,139
It was someone.

223
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:08,820
It always was.

224
00:09:09,350 --> 00:09:11,600
And only then did he remember his grandmother.

225
00:09:12,070 --> 00:09:16,919
"If you don't look, you won't find." He had looked.

226
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:19,449
Three forty in the morning.

227
00:09:19,470 --> 00:09:21,960
That's when he recorded the message for his brother.

228
00:09:22,210 --> 00:09:24,040
"I found her.

229
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:27,180
She's in all the photos.

230
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:33,019
And she knows that I know." After that,

231
00:09:33,090 --> 00:09:36,279
Rafael did the only thing left to do.

232
00:09:36,370 --> 00:09:38,069
He opened the front camera on his phone.

233
00:09:38,090 --> 00:09:42,940
And, without turning around, looked at the hallway behind him through the screen.

234
00:09:43,490 --> 00:09:45,040
She was there.

235
00:09:45,310 --> 00:09:46,629
One step behind.

236
00:09:46,650 --> 00:09:49,469
Level with his face.

237
00:09:49,490 --> 00:09:53,440
And, for the first time, she wasn't standing still.

238
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:55,149
The phone fell onto the hallway floor.

239
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:57,480
And kept recording.

240
00:09:57,550 --> 00:09:58,449
The ceiling.

241
00:09:58,470 --> 00:09:59,449
The light bulb swaying.

242
00:09:59,470 --> 00:10:01,580
His slippers on the floor.

243
00:10:01,730 --> 00:10:02,750
No sound.

244
00:10:02,770 --> 00:10:04,120
No scream.

245
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:06,000
Just the empty hallway.

246
00:10:06,250 --> 00:10:07,769
Lucas arrived in the morning.

247
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:09,609
The door was locked from the inside.

248
00:10:09,629 --> 00:10:10,969
The windows, closed.

249
00:10:10,990 --> 00:10:14,529
The phone, on the hallway floor.

250
00:10:14,550 --> 00:10:16,680
The battery, almost dead.

251
00:10:16,790 --> 00:10:20,120
And on the living room table, dozens of photos.

252
00:10:20,170 --> 00:10:22,920
Each one with a red circle.

253
00:10:23,050 --> 00:10:25,449
Rafael's case became a statistic.

254
00:10:25,470 --> 00:10:27,989
In Brazil alone, in twenty twenty-five,

255
00:10:28,009 --> 00:10:31,540
over eighty-four thousand people went missing.

256
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:33,560
Most are found.

257
00:10:33,670 --> 00:10:34,849
Some…

258
00:10:34,870 --> 00:10:35,840
never.

259
00:10:36,030 --> 00:10:38,529
The scientists were right about one thing.

260
00:10:38,550 --> 00:10:39,849
There really is a delay.

261
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:42,560
Except it's not in your brain.

262
00:10:42,730 --> 00:10:44,980
She was always in the images.

263
00:10:45,009 --> 00:10:46,500
From the beginning.

264
00:10:47,009 --> 00:10:49,069
Throughout this whole video…

265
00:10:49,090 --> 00:10:52,240
she was in every single scene.

266
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:54,080
Right in front of you.

267
00:10:54,190 --> 00:10:55,480
And neither you…

268
00:10:55,570 --> 00:10:56,069
nor Rafael…

269
00:10:56,090 --> 00:10:57,379
noticed.

270
00:10:59,610 --> 00:11:01,139
On the street.

271
00:11:02,950 --> 00:11:04,180
At the window.

272
00:11:05,910 --> 00:11:07,580
At the end of the hallway.

273
00:11:09,390 --> 00:11:11,259
By the kitchen door.

274
00:11:12,850 --> 00:11:14,639
In the corner of the bedroom.

275
00:11:16,390 --> 00:11:18,040
Behind the curtain.

276
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:21,620
In the middle of the hallway.

277
00:11:23,590 --> 00:11:24,820
Behind him.

278
00:11:25,570 --> 00:11:27,489
